  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result (config_027, 53.5% acc) uses PCA n2000 for RNA + ViT-L for image with concat fusion in a single-profile setting. RNA alone (48.5%) far outperforms image alone (22.7%), indicating RNA is the dominant signal and the image provides a modest complementary boost. We have only tested one RNA encoder (PCA, a linear method) and one image encoder (ViT-L). Uncertainty: Whether a learned nonlinear RNA representation (scvi_n200) captures biological structure that PCA misses, potentially improving both the RNA baseline and the multimodal ceiling. Question tested: config_021 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA n2000 to scvi_n200 while holding image encoder (ViT-L), fusion (concat), and profile setting (single) identical to config_027, cleanly isolating the RNA representation effect. Why this is the best next experiment: RNA is the stronger modality, so improving its representation is the highest-leverage single change. A direct A/B comparison against config_027 tells us whether to invest further in learned RNA encoders (scgpt, multiprofile) or whether PCA already captures most of the useful signal—critical information before committing budget to more complex multiprofile/aggregation configurations."
}

